      "message": "Question about backports: the generic username/password options in [cache] only exist from oslo.cache 2026.1 on. On 2024.1 (tag 2024.1-eom) only redis_username/redis_password are registered, so if this template is backported to stable/2024.1 as is, the credentials would be silently ignored. Since the spec lists 2024.1 and 2026.1 as targets, do we plan to backport this? If yes, either render the redis_-prefixed names (still accepted as deprecated aliases on 2026.1+, at the cost of a deprecation warning) or adapt the template in the backport. Fine on main either way.",
